{
	"_doc": "Ashfall Road (brief 2.4; v4: docs/decisions/tank.md). Owner: rules. Schema: TankContentSchema.validate_mission. The first 300 s are the 180 s hangar (the hull on its stand; the drills; the door opens in the last 10 s) and the 120 s roll-out (out of the door; it never halts), both WARMUP (BRIEF 4.6.8). Segments in plan order; every one is a lap-true plan phase (TankPlanBuilder). terrain: [distance_m, grade_pct] points, the course_profile format, interpolated linearly by the tank's distance into the segment and held past the last point; grades are before difficulty. encounters trigger when the tank has driven at_m metres into the Advance (far kinds in the far panel, near kinds from the bushes); obstacles stand at at_m in world space. A gun_line segment is a holding action in the UI: enemies {enemy, count, hold_m: [..]} on the move at long range, near {at_s, enemy, count} near threats by seconds into it; the boss segment has a near list too. Counts scale with the crew and difficulty (TankEncounters.crew_counts: the segment's total, taken from the lists in order, so each list puts first what the smallest crews must meet; min_crew: the entry is there only for crews of that size and up). end_hold_s: seconds the director waits after the objective is done before end_phase (the Autopilot's seating moves riders for the next segment; the Behemoth's death beat).",
